# v2 entrypoint — dramatiq replaces celery.
# concurrency=1 always: Demucs is memory-heavy AND the LLM gateway builds its
# async client per call/loop — multiple threads sharing a process would reuse a
# client across event loops. Pin a single worker (CLAUDE.md worker gotcha).
#
# Queues (AR23, story 2.5): one dev worker drains ALL four queues, so dev
# behavior is functionally identical to prod (every message gets processed by
# one process). The W1/W2 split lives in docker/docker-compose.prod.yml.
#   analysis-paid : pro/credits analysis + all 5 auxiliary actors
#   analysis-free : free/anon analysis (sole declarer = analyze_audio_job)
#   coach         : coach_reply
#   maintenance   : provisioned-but-empty (Epic 3/4 add sweep_retention/send_email)
# `default` is dropped — no producer remains after story 2.5. If you run against
# a long-lived dev Redis that may hold stray `default` messages, append `default`.
worker: python -m dramatiq app.dramatiq_app --processes 1 --threads 1 --queues coach analysis-paid analysis-free maintenance
